Notebook[{
Cell["WolframExample: Rust libraries from the Wolfram Language", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"383222bb-428e-4ebe-b875-a9667fe3c81b"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook exercises the WolframExample paclet, whose functions are \
implemented in Rust (see WolframExample/Libs). Evaluate it top to bottom.

If the setup section reports a missing paclet, build the library first:
    cd WolframExample && cargo wl build\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8050a19c-28ae-438f-8199-9296e8aa831e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6a217766-ad84-44b1-9b0f-fe370bca88c9"],

Cell["\<\
Both paclets \[LongDash] the hand-written WolframExample and the generated \
WolframExampleLib \[LongDash] sit in this notebook's parent directory, so one \
PacletDirectoryLoad registers both.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25cb9acd-c5d2-4aa3-a21b-529343b226f1"],

Cell["PacletDirectoryLoad[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c9c6df11-ffc9-40c1-ab70-b22ba796a92a"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExample\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9dbd754e-d5c1-4c78-8419-9fbc7c9c4993"],

Cell["\<\
The library paclet holds nothing but the compiled dylibs and a generated \
Functions.wl loader:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2656b324-0219-4b36-9b79-ad2ccf86e23d"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"852f4c8b-5b8a-4ab7-b017-0ff6d953169f"],

Cell["Needs[\"WolframExample`\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"95eec9a3-da0a-4dee-ad2f-5e1a89d47011"],

Cell["Everything the package exports:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"855d2100-a95a-43e4-a934-c2703f17f01c"],

Cell["?WolframExample`*", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"11c6bc49-4aed-4088-9b49-d5d60632ddb9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Math", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8d2f498e-0484-4bf4-aa4d-21c698ab30d7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scalars and arrays", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"8aa93e2d-596f-4e68-8ecb-087a7fe1b1ba"],

Cell["\<\
A plain Rust function over two f64s. Arguments and result cross as raw \
MArgument scalars \[LongDash] no serialization at all.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36ae3e12-93b3-4ad1-a7f0-456edc5ac052"],

Cell["ExampleAdd[2, 3]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"16455868-f7b0-481e-8703-5e97274bf63b"],

Cell["\<\
NumericArrays are read zero-copy: Rust sees the kernel's own memory, no copy \
and no conversion. Lists are packed into a Real64 NumericArray by the wrapper \
first.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"241b8627-03b7-413f-9a7a-5ef2a987fbf1"],

Cell["ExampleDot[{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5f8694b9-60c6-4b5e-83fa-a94f7b970d41"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleDot[
    NumericArray[Range[1., 100000.], \"Real64\"],
    NumericArray[Range[100000., 1., -1.], \"Real64\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e1ec51aa-2790-441d-a67f-d0b319e870cc"],

Cell["Same call, timed against the kernel's own Dot:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b774456c-2f5b-41b2-b92b-a2b89f34ef85"],

Cell["\<\
With[{a = Range[1., 100000.], b = Range[100000., 1., -1.]},
    {
        \"Rust\" -> First @ RepeatedTiming @ ExampleDot[a, b],
        \"Kernel\" -> First @ RepeatedTiming @ Dot[a, b]
    }
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ed962bda-d1ec-4357-a833-2769dffa323b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Structs and enums", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4f863aab-1297-40fb-a51b-75275a786ce8"],

Cell["\<\
Structured arguments cross as WXF. A Rust struct is an Association keyed by \
its field names; the wrapper here presents Wolfram-style capitalized keys.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9296dba1-569f-4484-a633-99a3541c083c"],

Cell["ExampleSymmetricPoint[<|\"X\" -> 10, \"Y\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5a4971b8-0271-4478-92cf-824265994834"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleArea goes through a Rust enum \[LongDash] one function, one match, two \
shapes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0e62ab7-1b6f-48e3-bdb5-eef1dcd4de32"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> 1|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a8800c1b-074e-4f26-bd2d-a04174be6505"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Width\" -> 10, \"Height\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"646df835-baf5-47f5-9109-781dfbfe0a07"],

Cell["Table[ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> r|>], {r, 1, 5}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ef94f4ea-b927-4d12-8a24-d97e1f20b40d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Errors", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"66c32edc-c949-45d3-8cf0-7e758aa549f8"],

Cell["\<\
A Rust Result<f64, String> comes back as {\"Ok\", value} or {\"Err\", \
message}; the wrapper turns the error branch into a Failure.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d746d3cf-a1d2-45c5-b3a1-2cdf22b416cc"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[10, 4]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"56e5e05f-0501-4f0b-b32d-fbe85c33c606"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cf823aa1-4857-4324-9cbd-58ff1e723e97"],

Cell["So the usual Failure handling applies:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"98fdf6b4-1ccc-4206-88a7-afced4894a4c"],

Cell["\<\
FailureQ /@ {ExampleSafeDivide[1, 2], ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8b7b40bf-8c8a-4aed-88b0-882d004496f0"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["DuckDB", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"03048775-a585-4acf-a4f2-980b6d430489"],

Cell["\<\
An entire embedded SQL engine, statically linked into the library \[LongDash] \
nothing to install. Query results come back as Arrow and are decoded into a \
Tabular.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d37f4ae-69ca-48bd-a362-1bad20ebfe24"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scoped connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6f6c1da5-fdcb-4eea-bdb8-bb57d6bae4f0"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute opens a connection, applies the function to it, and closes it \
again \[LongDash] even if the body fails.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"909a57d8-5ac0-427f-8438-89db6f919f7f"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT 42 AS answer\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b0e036e0-29b7-4bf7-85c5-58d33316250b"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n::INTEGER AS id,
            (n * 1.5)::DOUBLE AS score,
            'item_' || n AS label,
            n % 2 = 0 AS is_even
     FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n)\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2c9d1eae-adfe-4414-b7e2-e42153c63e01"],

Cell["\<\
The result is an ordinary Tabular, so the usual operations work:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e145c63c-07c8-4d32-b0ba-cfa18e393a62"],

Cell["\<\
tab = DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 100) t(n)\"] &];
{Length[tab], Total[tab[[All, \"n\"]]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"51ca526f-e33a-4d40-b682-66f6b45b5e0a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Parameters", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"32206d56-9422-441c-96a0-65b29450b930"],

Cell["\<\
Values are bound to the ? placeholders in order, so nothing is interpolated \
into the SQL string.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"baf03626-8e30-404c-9d58-1f828e806952"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n) WHERE n > ?\", {2}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"534145eb-acb7-4342-8936-112e2c7c48c1"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT ?::INTEGER + ?::INTEGER AS total\", {20, 22}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"195d9d0f-df46-4637-9244-06b6dee8ea73"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Explicit connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b43a1535-3710-4e48-9914-da4a890ee3c1"],

Cell["\<\
For several statements against the same database, hold the handle yourself. \
Here an on-disk file, which persists after disconnecting.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5342da2-bba7-46cf-b6bf-7a61cf3b23fe"],

Cell["\<\
file = FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"wolfram-example.duckdb\"}];
Quiet[DeleteFile[file]];
conn = DuckDBConnect[\"duckdb:///\" <> file]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"58fe05b9-f330-4c6f-a93d-f6d0863c6756"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn,
    \"CREATE TABLE fruit AS SELECT * FROM (VALUES (1, 'apple'), (2, 'pear')) \
v(id, name)\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e87d1655-5746-4756-8d68-720e6ba8a9bc"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn, \"INSERT INTO fruit VALUES (?, ?)\", {3, \"plum\"}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7053ced8-5541-4c30-b0f1-3cfae0df44fc"],

Cell["DuckDBQuery[conn, \"SELECT * FROM fruit ORDER BY id\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"451e098d-1b46-4a04-8293-912cc712e422"],

Cell["DuckDBDisconnect[conn]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fa6e2ed6-e398-405c-aa77-d27acab7637f"],

Cell["Reopening the same file shows the rows are still there:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b6e39a11-7436-44d0-899d-4da81c46f6fe"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb:///\" <> file,
    DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT count(*) AS rows FROM fruit\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9d27c6fa-8f2d-48f5-a1a0-b6ab2b1dfc82"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Failures", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ac254b44-b37f-4c8d-b2fb-1ab313651a38"],

Cell["\<\
Errors from the engine arrive as Failure objects carrying DuckDB's own \
message, and propagate on their own.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7798b574-da48-476e-9a83-15c2d88a43f5"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT * FROM no_such_table\"] \
&]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0a8f6709-654d-4a6c-aff1-14138932b6b7"],

Cell["\<\
A handle that has been closed is no longer in the Rust-side registry:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e007224d-49b8-4141-9d09-d4fdfda71e5f"],

Cell["\<\
With[{c = DuckDBConnect[]},
    DuckDBDisconnect[c];
    DuckDBQuery[c, \"SELECT 1\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f9112e4f-e5f2-4fdb-bfeb-3edea77e8ae5"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The raw library", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2e2b434a-b079-4fc2-a5d2-a0980cb53b9a"],

Cell["\<\
The wrappers in Kernel/WolframExample.wl are a thin layer over an association \
of LibraryFunctions, keyed \"namespace::rust_name\". Anything without a \
wrapper is still one lookup away.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"461e3839-eff5-4171-8444-7517147be0f5"],

Cell["Keys[WolframExampleFunctions[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"42f4ecf7-e610-4f1e-a5e6-685f71192060"],

Cell["\<\
inactive_sum builds an expression in Rust and returns it unevaluated:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ee496304-97bc-4987-b220-4e74211f7726"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1d88b1c2-12a1-4603-b60d-102b220d712e"],

Cell["\<\
Activate[WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9cbb5c73-ed3d-40fa-9c90-13890a5317e8"],

Cell["\<\
A panic on the Rust side is caught at the boundary and returned as a Failure \
\[LongDash] it does not take the kernel down:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46a329f3-13cc-47f2-a298-9f8377167a78"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::panic\"][]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"482df834-9ecd-4029-a285-fb460e7b48e1"],

Cell["\<\
And the signatures of everything that was packaged, straight from the \
generated Artifacts.wl asset:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bf57807b-cecd-42e7-84c0-059f13787161"],

Cell["\<\
Get[PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"][\"AssetLocation\", \"Artifacts\"]] //
    Map[Query[{\"Name\", \"Signatures\"}]] // Dataset\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e4f1a59e-d543-46c5-a85f-3a4dba64ca63"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Rebuilding", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a3b2fe7c-17f6-46f6-87f0-064a7d633d14"],

Cell["\<\
After editing the Rust source, rebuild from the paclet directory. The dylibs \
are content-hashed, so a rebuilt library gets a new file name \[LongDash] \
quit the kernel to pick it up.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf1657b5-1a03-42e5-9f76-d2ae16105436"],

Cell["\<\
ExternalEvaluate[{\"Shell\",
    \"ProcessDirectory\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"WolframExample\"}],
    \"ProcessEnvironment\" -> <|\"PATH\" -> Environment[\"PATH\"]|>},
   \"cargo wl build --release\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"75225890-da12-4a4b-9665-b610ebbbb4ac"]
}, Open  ]]
},
WindowTitle->"WolframExample Tour",
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (May 6, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"913badbc-3a5c-4b27-9daf-1544278ea03d"
]
